      "writtenOn": "2022-07-08T19:18:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we add it to `SkRuntimeEffect.h` as a public method, then we\u0027re exposing it to all our clients (Chrome, Android, Flutter, etc) and endorsing it as \"this is a safe thing to rely on.\" Having clients fish the `SkSL::Program` out of a runtime effect isn\u0027t something we want them to start relying on :) \n\nIn other words, if a function or method is accessible from `include/`, users expect that\u0027s it\u0027s an OK thing to use. The Priv classes are in `src/` (not `include/`), so users cannot rely on anything inside.",
